      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: 'Conditional aborts are a key feature in order to reevaluate the behavior
        tree. The Agent behavior tree uses a Lower Priority Conditional Abort to
        continuously check if the enemy is within sight. As soon as the enemy is
        in sight the abort will trigger and the agent will start to seek towards
        the enemy.

        See this page for more information on conditional aborts:

        https://opsive.com/support/documentation/behavior-designer-pro/conditional-aborts/

'
